      "id": "h1-cache-sim",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "skills": [
        "sy-memory"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "cache-lines"
      ],
      "pace": 1500,
      "title": "A cache simulator",
      "prose": "Turn this level's hand counts into code. A cache has `num_lines` lines of 64 bytes, in sets of `ways` lines. Byte address `a` is in line `a / 64`, which lives in set `(a / 64) % (num_lines / ways)`. A full set drops its least recently used line.",
      "question": "Write `count_misses`: start empty and return the number of misses.",
      "widget": {
        "kind": "code",
        "language": "cpp",
        "starter": "#include <vector>\n\n// A cache of num_lines lines of 64 bytes, in sets of `ways` lines each (num_lines is a multiple of ways).\n// The line holding byte address a is a / 64 and it lives in set (a / 64) % (num_lines / ways).\n// A full set drops its least recently used line. Start empty. Return the number of misses.\nint count_misses(int num_lines, int ways, const std::vector<int>& addresses) {\n    int misses = 0;\n    for (int a : addresses) {\n        (void)a;\n        ++misses;     // TODO: an access whose line is already in its set is a hit\n    }\n    return misses;\n}\n",
        "solution": "#include <list>\n#include <vector>\n\nint count_misses(int num_lines, int ways, const std::vector<int>& addresses) {\n    int sets = num_lines / ways;\n    std::vector<std::list<int>> cache(sets);      // front = most recently used\n    int misses = 0;\n    for (int a : addresses) {\n        int line = a / 64;\n        std::list<int>& set = cache[line % sets];\n        bool hit = false;\n        for (auto it = set.begin(); it != set.end(); ++it) {\n            if (*it == line) { set.erase(it); hit = true; break; }\n        }\n        if (!hit) {\n            ++misses;\n            if (static_cast<int>(set.size()) == ways) set.pop_back();\n        }\n        set.push_front(line);\n    }\n    return misses;\n}\n",
        "examples": [
          {
            "call": "count_misses",
            "args": [
